```

## Staying updated

### Layer 1 — libraries
- Manual: `just upgrade` (runs `uv lock --upgrade`), then `uv sync`.
- Automatic: `.github/workflows/update-deps.yml` opens a weekly PR with the
  upgraded lockfile, gated by CI.
- Granular: `renovate.json` manages libraries **plus** GitHub Actions, the
  Docker base image, pre-commit hook versions, the pinned `uv` version, and
  `.python-version`.{% if automerge_safe_updates %} Patch/dev/CI updates auto-merge after CI passes; the AI stack and majors are held for review.{% else %} Nothing auto-merges — every update is a reviewed PR.{% endif %}

### Layer 2 — the template
- Manual: `just template-update` (runs `copier update`).
- Automatic: `.github/workflows/template-update.yml` opens a monthly PR with the
  latest template version applied.

> Both layers open **PRs gated by CI** — they never push to `main`. A green CI on
> an upgrade means "tests pass," not "behaviour is unchanged," so the AI
> frameworks in particular are always reviewed by a human.

