## API keys / service tokens

Machine clients authenticate with **API keys** instead of a user JWT. A key is created
inside an org and is shown **once** at creation; only a SHA-256 hash of the secret is
stored (the plaintext `prefix` is kept for lookup and display).

```text
POST   /orgs/{org_id}/api-keys        mint a key (returns the full secret ONCE)
GET    /orgs/{org_id}/api-keys        list this org's keys (prefixes only, never the secret)
DELETE /orgs/{org_id}/api-keys/{id}   revoke a key
GET    /whoami                        resolve the caller (accepts a JWT OR an API key)
```

Pass a key as the `X-API-Key` header. The `get_principal` dependency in
`app.api_keys.dependencies` accepts **either** a logged-in user (JWT) **or** a valid API
key — it looks the key up by prefix, verifies the hash in constant time, rejects revoked
or expired keys, stamps `last_used_at`, and binds the acting identity + org.

