## Billing & entitlements (provider-agnostic)

Payments go through a **hexagonal port**: `app.billing.ports.PaymentsPort` is the app's-needs
contract; `app.billing.adapters` holds the **Stripe** and **Razorpay** implementations; the
active one is selected by `PAYMENTS_PROVIDER` (default `{{ payments_provider }}`). The router,
entitlements, webhook, and `Subscription` model speak only the port and the normalized
`PaymentEvent` — they never import a vendor SDK. Each org is a provider customer
(`organizations.payments_customer_id`, created lazily on first checkout/portal access). Plans
map to features via `app.billing.entitlements`, gated by a `require_feature(...)` dependency.

```text
POST   /orgs/{org_id}/billing/checkout-session   start provider checkout (returns a URL)
POST   /orgs/{org_id}/billing/portal-session     open the provider customer portal (returns a URL)
GET    /orgs/{org_id}/billing/subscription       the org's subscription (local row, else live lookup)
DELETE /orgs/{org_id}/billing/subscription       cancel the org's subscription
GET    /orgs/{org_id}/billing/usage              example route gated by require_feature(...)
POST   /billing/webhook                           provider events (signature-verified, idempotent)
```

The org-scoped routes reuse the tenancy membership dependency. The webhook reads the active
provider's signature header, verifies the **signature** via the port (rejecting forgeries with
`400`), and **dedupes** replayed events by `(provider, event_id)`, then syncs a `Subscription`
row from normalized subscription-lifecycle events.

Configure the active provider's credentials in your environment — **test-mode keys only**,
never hard-coded:
- **Stripe** (`PAYMENTS_PROVIDER=stripe`): `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`,
  `STRIPE_PLAN_TO_PRICE` (internal plan → Stripe Price id).
- **Razorpay** (`PAYMENTS_PROVIDER=razorpay`): `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`, `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET`,
  `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `RAZORPAY_PLAN_TO_PLAN_ID` (internal plan → Razorpay Plan id),
  `RAZORPAY_PORTAL_URL`.

**Adding a payment provider** = implement `PaymentsPort` in `app.billing.adapters`, register it
in `app.billing.provider`, and add its key to the `payments_provider` choices — see AGENTS.md.
The one provider-specific boundary is the **frontend checkout handoff**: `start_checkout`
returns each provider's own hosted-checkout redirect URL.

{% endif %}
