## Admin / control panel (sqladmin)

A [sqladmin](https://aminalaee.dev/sqladmin/) control panel is mounted at **`/admin`**, gated
behind **superuser-only** authentication — it is never mounted open. The `AuthenticationBackend`
verifies logins against the `user` table with fastapi-users' own password hashing and admits
only **active superusers**; the validated user id is held in a signed session and re-checked
against the database on every request, so deactivating or demoting a user revokes panel access
immediately.

```bash
# Promote a user to superuser so they can reach /admin (e.g. with psql):
#   UPDATE "user" SET is_superuser = true WHERE email = 'you@example.com';
# then open http://localhost:8000/admin and sign in with that account.
```

Model views are registered for the capabilities this service ships — users always,
{% if include_tenancy or include_rbac or include_api_keys or include_billing or include_webhooks %}organizations + memberships, {% endif %}{% if include_billing %}subscriptions, {% endif %}{% if include_api_keys %}API keys, {% endif %}{% if include_webhooks %}webhook endpoints, {% endif %}{% if include_audit %}and the audit log (read-only / append-only) {% endif %}— with
secrets **redacted** from the list, the detail page and the edit form: password
{% if include_api_keys %}and API-key hashes{% else %}hashes{% endif %}{% if include_webhooks %}, webhook signing secrets{% endif %}{% if include_billing %}, and provider customer / subscription ids{% endif %} are
never exposed. The session-signing secret reuses `USERS_JWT_SECRET`. To administer another
table, add a `ModelView` in `app/admin/views.py` and register it in `register_model_views`.

