## Observability (OpenTelemetry — three pillars)

Full OpenTelemetry: **traces, metrics and logs** export over OTLP, correlated. FastAPI and
httpx are auto-instrumented{% if include_db or include_users or include_tenancy or include_rbac or include_api_keys or include_billing or include_audit or include_webhooks or include_admin %}, along with SQLAlchemy{% endif %}{% if include_cache or include_jobs or include_webhooks %} and Redis{% endif %}; every
structlog line emitted inside a request carries the active span's `trace_id` / `span_id`, so a
log links straight to its trace.

**Nothing exports until you configure it** — set `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` (e.g.
`http://localhost:4318`) and the three pillars start flowing; leave it unset and a fresh service
runs clean with no collector. Error reporting is opt-in too: set `SENTRY_DSN` to turn on Sentry
(unhandled exceptions are recorded on the span regardless).

Endpoints (always mounted):

```
GET /healthz   # liveness — 200 while the process is up
GET /readyz    # readiness — probes {% if include_db or include_users or include_tenancy or include_rbac or include_api_keys or include_billing or include_audit or include_webhooks or include_admin %}the database{% endif %}{% if (include_db or include_users or include_tenancy or include_rbac or include_api_keys or include_billing or include_audit or include_webhooks or include_admin) and (include_cache or include_jobs or include_webhooks) %} + {% endif %}{% if include_cache or include_jobs or include_webhooks %}Redis{% endif %}{% if not (include_db or include_users or include_tenancy or include_rbac or include_api_keys or include_billing or include_audit or include_webhooks or include_admin or include_cache or include_jobs or include_webhooks) %}its dependencies{% endif %}, 503 if any is down
GET /metrics   # Prometheus process/runtime metrics (HTTP request metrics export via OTLP)
```

### Local stack

`just observe` brings up a full local view via a compose profile — **OTel Collector +
Prometheus + Tempo + Loki + Grafana**, datasources and a starter dashboard pre-provisioned:

```bash
just observe                                          # docker compose --profile observability up
# then point the app at the collector, in .env:
#   OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector:4318   # compose `api`
#   OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318        # `just run` on the host
```

Open Grafana at <http://localhost:3000> (anonymous admin) — metrics in Prometheus, traces in
Tempo, logs in Loki, all correlated. Stack config lives in `observability/`.

