## Container image & supply chain

`.github/workflows/release-image.yml` publishes a **signed, provenanced** image to GHCR on
every push to `main` (and on `v*` tags). The pipeline: build the digest-pinned, reproducible
image (`SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`) → attach a **CycloneDX SBOM** → Trivy-scan → **keyless-sign** with
cosign (Sigstore via GitHub OIDC — no long-lived keys) → attach **SLSA build provenance**.
No secrets to configure; it uses the workflow's `GITHUB_TOKEN` + OIDC. Delete the workflow if
this service doesn't ship a container.

Verify a pulled image (`OWNER`/`REPO` lowercased, `DIGEST` = `sha256:...`):

```bash
cosign verify ghcr.io/OWNER/REPO@DIGEST \
  --certificate-identity-regexp '^https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/' \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com
gh attestation verify oci://ghcr.io/OWNER/REPO@DIGEST --owner OWNER
```

Actions are SHA-pinned (Renovate keeps the digests current); the Trivy scan is report-only by
default — flip it to `exit-code: "1"` to block a publish on a fixable HIGH/CRITICAL CVE. The
SLSA-provenance step runs on public repos (on Free/Pro/Team the attestation API is public-only);
on **GitHub Enterprise Cloud** drop the `if:` on that step to attest private repos too.

## Working with Claude

This service is born Claude-ready. `AGENTS.md` holds the conventions and decision
rules; `CLAUDE.md` just `@AGENTS.md`-imports them and lists the command/subagent
surface. Drive it with:

- `/feature "<what to build>"` — implement a feature end-to-end, then self-review.
- `/check` — run every gate (ruff + mypy + pytest).

Two guardrails run automatically: a PreToolUse hook **blocks `pip install`** (use
`uv add`), and a PostToolUse hook ruff-formats Python on save. The `code-reviewer`
and `build-judge` subagents are read-only — you own edits and commits.

## Notes
- Type checking is `mypy`; switch to Astral's `ty` once it's 1.0:
  `uv remove --dev mypy && uv add --dev ty --prerelease allow`.
- One agent framework per service — they cannot co-resolve. To switch, re-run
  `copier update` and re-answer `agent_framework`, then re-lock.
